---
/* The owner's editor, at /edit.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Wiring only. The panel itself is @shaahink/sitekit/editor — every control,
   every string, every rule about what an owner may change lives there, and
   this site deliberately owns none of it. Four hand-maintained copies of one
   admin screen is what sitekit exists to prevent; CLAUDE.md's "no design
   system in the kit" rule governs the pages a visitor sees, not this one.

   So this file should never change again. If improving the editor ever means
   editing it, the boundary is in the wrong place and the boundary is what
   should move.

   Its own route, on purpose. Google Identity Services needs to load a script
   from accounts.google.com, open an iframe there, talk to it, and inject its
   own <style> — and adding all of that to the site's global CSP would loosen
   the posture on every public page to serve a page almost nobody visits. Astro
   emits the policy per page, so the looser directives are attached here and
   nowhere else, and the public pages stay untouched by construction rather
   than by a path rule somebody has to keep correct.

   Deliberately not wrapped in Base.astro: no nav, no footer, no review-mode
   gate, and no locale — the panel's chrome is one language and the content it
   edits carries its own direction (every field is dir="auto", so a Persian or
   Arabic field reads right-to-left inside a left-to-right panel). This is a
   tool, not part of the site.

   The route is /edit here because this template builds with format
   "directory". A site that sets build.format: "file" serves it at /edit.html
   instead, and its robots.txt disallow has to say so. */

/* The panel's stylesheet is copied into public/ by `npm run editor` (the kit
   ships the copier; CI regenerates and diffs it) and linked below rather than
   imported. Astro collects every processed stylesheet's hash into *every*
   page's style-src, so importing it here would add the editor's hash to the
   CSP of every public page — harmless, but it would mean the public policy is
   no longer provably untouched. */

/* Typed optional because CSP can be switched off; astro.config turns it on for
   this site, so on this route it is always there. */
const csp = Astro.csp!;

/* Everything Google Identity Services needs, on this route only. The values
   restate astro.config's directives rather than assuming a merge, so the
   result is correct whether Astro appends to them or replaces them — which
   also means this block changes when the site's own CSP does, and only then. */
csp.insertScriptResource("https://accounts.google.com");
csp.insertDirective("frame-src https://accounts.google.com");
csp.insertDirective("connect-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com");
csp.insertDirective("img-src 'self' data: https://lh3.googleusercontent.com");

/* ⚠ Those three lines restate what astro.config sets globally, with Google's
   origins added. Astro *replaces* a directive rather than merging into it, so
   anything the site adds to connect-src or img-src there has to be repeated
   here or it is silently dropped on this route. When the analytics tag goes
   live, https://sk-stats.vercel.app joins connect-src in both places. This is
   the one part of the editor that is genuinely per-site, and it changes only
   when the site's own CSP does. */

/* Naming any element-kind style source moves this page from `style-src` to
   `style-src-elem`, and that directive does *not* inherit `style-src`'s
   sources — so 'self' has to be restated or the panel's own stylesheet is
   blocked on the one page that needs it.

   'unsafe-inline' is here for the <style> Google Identity Services injects,
   but CSP ignores 'unsafe-inline' whenever a hash is present and Astro puts
   the build's stylesheet hashes here. So it does nothing today. It states the
   intent, and whether GIS needs it at all is genuinely unknown — recent
   versions render the button inside an iframe from accounts.google.com, which
   frame-src already covers. */
csp.insertStyleResource({ resource: "'self'", kind: "element" });
csp.insertStyleResource({ resource: "'unsafe-inline'", kind: "element" });
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Edit</title>
    <!-- Nothing here belongs in an index, and there is no public content on
         this page to find anyway. -->
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/editor-panel.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main data-sk-editor>
      <!-- The panel builds itself from the content schemas; without
           JavaScript there is nothing to show and nothing to promise. -->
      <noscript>
        <p>The editor needs JavaScript. Everything else on this site doesn't.</p>
      </noscript>
    </main>

    <script>
      import { mountEditor } from "@shaahink/sitekit/editor";

      const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-sk-editor]");
      if (root) mountEditor(root);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
